/* ======================================================================================================================
   v25 add-on: the container ports of New York and New Jersey (纽约-新泽西港) on the New York City map
   - the real container terminals on their real quays (OSM coastline and terminal parcels; crane counts from the operators'
     published fleets, positions spread along the real wharves):
       Port Newark–Elizabeth: the Elizabeth Channel north bank (Port Newark Container Terminal, 13 cranes, straddle carriers),
       the south bank and the Newark Bay front (the largest terminal, 24 cranes, straddle carriers), the Newark Bay and South
       Elizabeth Channel front (15 cranes, rubber-tyred gantries), the Port Newark Channel barge terminal;
       Port Jersey, Bayonne (12 cranes, RTGs); Howland Hook, Staten Island (7 cranes, straddle carriers); Red Hook, Brooklyn
       (Pier 10, 2 cranes, reach stackers).
   - ship-to-shore A-frame quay cranes (instanced; boom down over a ship, raised on idle ones), animated trolleys, ropes,
     spreaders and boxes; container yards (instanced stacks, per-container colours in the shader, generic mixed colours, no
     markings; one box per block far away), RTGs, straddle carriers, reach stackers, chassis, drayage trucks, berthed container
     ships (140–400 m), a container barge, tugs, high-mast floodlights (lit yards at night), crane and aviation lights, gates,
     quay walls, the on-dock intermodal rail yards (double-stack well-car trains);
   - container ships under way with their tugs: from the Lower Bay through the Narrows and the Upper Bay, the Kill Van Kull under
     the Bayonne Bridge, into Newark Bay (Elizabeth / Newark) or the Arthur Kill (Howland Hook), or up to Port Jersey; ships at
     anchor in the Upper and Lower Bay.
   - real buildings stay as they are (the app draws them); the terminal surface is a paved platform at quay level.
   Data (zones, berths, yard blocks, masts, gates, internal roads, yard tracks, routes) is precomputed from the app's own OSM
   data (nyc/nyport/tools/prep.py). World x east, y north; three.js position (x, h, -y). Traffic keeps right.
   No company names, logos or liveries anywhere.
   ====================================================================================================================== */
